      "id": 1,
      "text": "Groton was founded in 1817 as the Town of Division before New England settlers renamed it after Groton, Massachusetts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groton%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1849, Charles and Lyman Perrigo started the first blast furnace and machine factories that helped shape Groton’s early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grotonny.gov/historical-facts",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first library opened in 1834, making Groton one of the earliest communities in the Finger Lakes region to establish a public lending library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grotonny.gov/historical-facts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Groton High School earned a place on the National Register of Historic Places in 1994, preserving its historic campus for future generations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groton%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
